  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190805": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Bagpipes (part-time)",
      "description": "Department: The College of Wooster Location: Wooster, OH The College of Wooster seeks applications for a part-time Bagpipes instructor beginning October 2026. Primary duties would include: · Teaching weekly lessons to Music majors and non-majors · Coach Bagpipes within the Pipe Band · Maintain Bagpipe-specific inventory, including instruments and accessories.  Order new items as needed through the Music Department · Work with the Scottish Drumming instructor and the Highland Dance instructor Degree in Music strongly preferred. Candidate must demonstrate evidence of successful performance and teaching, as well as the ability to be a congenial colleague.  The ideal candidate will have a successful and ongoing record of instruction of Bagpipes, demonstrated success in recruiting and retaining students, and have reached Grade 1 or Professional solo ranks. Applicants should submit the following materials: · A letter of application · A curriculum vitae or resume · Names of three professional references with contact information · Links to recent audio and/or video performances and/or teaching If you have questions regarding Interfolio, please contact Melissa Puster, mpuster@wooster.edu. Questions about the position should be directed to Jeff Gershman, jgershman@wooster.edu. Start Date: October 12, 2026 Application Deadline: Screening will begin immediately and will continue until a qualified candidate is selected, with preference given to applications received before August 31."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189925": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Flute",
      "description": "Department: The College of Wooster Location: Wooster, OH Job Area: Woodwinds Job Title: Adjunct Instructor of Flute Rank: Adjunct Instructor Part-time position for a flute instructor beginning August, 2026. Primary duties include teaching weekly flute lessons to both majors and non-majors, as well as coaching ensemble(s) as needed. There are opportunities on campus for recitals and other public performances. Every other Fall semester (the next being Fall 2027), there is also the possibility of teaching the Flute portion of our Woodwind Methods sequence for Music Education majors. Qualifications: Master’s degree or equivalent professional teaching experience strongly preferred. Candidate must demonstrate evidence of successful teaching and the ability to engage students at various levels of experience and skill. Preferred qualifications: Demonstrated success in recruiting and retaining students is highly desired. Start Date: August 19, 2026 Application Deadline: Screening will begin immediately and will continue until a qualified candidate is selected, with preference given to applications received before August 1, 2026. What to send: Interested applicants should upload the following documents (PDF format preferred): 1) Letter of interest 2) Curriculum vitae 3) Names and contact information for three references. 4) Links to recent audio and/or video performances should be included in the application. The College of Wooster is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer and seeks to attract an academically and culturally diverse faculty. We welcome applications from members of groups traditionally underrepresented in the field, and applicants are encouraged to state in their cover letter how they will enhance the diversity of offerings and educational experiences if hired."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190808": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Scottish Drumming (part-time)",
      "description": "Department: The College of Wooster Location: Wooster, OH The College of Wooster seeks applications for a part time Scottish Drumming instructor beginning October 2026. Primary duties would include: · Teaching weekly lessons to Music majors and non-majors · Coach Scottish Percussion within the Pipe Band · Maintain Scottish Drumming-specific inventory, including instruments and accessories.  Order new items as needed through the Music Department · Work with the Bagpipes instructor and the Highland Dance instructor Degree in Music strongly preferred. Candidate must demonstrate evidence of successful performance and teaching, as well as the ability to be a congenial colleague. The ideal candidate will have a successful and ongoing record of instruction of Scottish Drumming, demonstrated success in recruiting and retaining students, and have reached Grade 2, Grade 1, or Professional solo ranks. Applicants should submit the following materials: · A letter of application · A curriculum vitae or resume · Names of three professional references with contact information · Links to recent audio and/or video performances and/or teaching If you have questions regarding Interfolio, please contact Melissa Puster, mpuster@wooster.edu. Questions about the position should be directed to Jeff Gershman, jgershman@wooster.edu. Start Date: October 12, 2026 Application Deadline: Screening will begin immediately and will continue until a qualified candidate is selected, with preference given to applications received before August 31."
    },
    "https://wooster.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204174": {
      "title": "Bus Driver, PT",
      "description": "The College of Wooster\nJob Posting: Bus Driver, PT The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: Bus Driver, PT Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Bus Driver, PT Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Materials Mgmt/Transportation Locations: Wooster, OH Posted: Aug 27, 2026 Closes: Oct 25, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Part-time Non-Exempt Position ID: 204174 Share About The College of Wooster: Wooster offers an excellent, comprehensive liberal arts education, culminating in a rigorous senior project, in which each student works one-on-one with a faculty mentor to conceive, organize and complete a significant research project on a topic of the student's own choosing. Through this distinctive program, every Wooster student develops abilities valued by employers and graduate schools alike: independent judgment, analytical ability, creativity, project-management and time-management skills, and strong written and oral communication skills. Founded in 1866, the college enrolls approximately 2,000 students. The College offers a comprehensive benefits program that includes: Health, Dental, Retirement, and Tuition Remission for eligible positions. Job Description: Summary: The Transportation Services Driver provides safe and reliable transportation services for the College community by operating buses, shuttles, and service vehicles. The position ensures compliance with transportation regulations, conducts vehicle inspections, maintains accurate records, assists passengers, and supports the maintenance, cleanliness, and operational readiness of the College's transportation fleet. Essential Departmental Duties and Responsibilities: Safely operate College buses, shuttles, and service vehicles, including route planning, trip coordination, and passenger assistance. Ensure compliance with state, federal, and DOT regulations through required inspections, documentation, and maintenance of driver logs. Complete and maintain accurate trip records, including mileage, hours worked, expenses, inspection reports, and related documentation. Perform routine vehicle inspections and safety checks, identifying and reporting maintenance and repair needs. Assist with preventative maintenance and minor repairs, including replacing filters, belts, bulbs, wiper blades, and interior components as approved. Maintain vehicle readiness by monitoring fuel and fluid levels, onboard safety equipment, and operational systems. Fuel, service, and clean buses and shuttles, including interior and exterior detailing and restroom maintenance. Maintain bus fleet records, including fuel consumption, maintenance activities, supplies inventory, and purchasing documentation. Manage transportation-related resources, including purchasing cards, passes, supplies, and destination route databases. Maintain bus garage facilities and inventory, ensuring vehicles, equipment, and supplies are organized, stocked, and operational. Other duties as assigned Requirements: Education and/or Experience: High school diploma or general education degree (GED); or one to three years related experience and/or training. Must have valid Ohio CDL driver's license (passenger CDL). Knowledge: Safe operation of buses, shuttles, and passenger vehicles. Department of Transportation (DOT), state, and federal transportation regulations. Vehicle inspection procedures, preventative maintenance practices, and fleet safety standards. Recordkeeping, trip documentation, and compliance reporting requirements. Skills: Operating commercial passenger vehicles safely and efficiently. Route planning, navigation, and trip coordination. Conducting vehicle inspections and identifying maintenance concerns. Maintaining accurate records, logs, and transportation documentation. Abilities : Work independently and exercise sound judgment in changing travel conditions. Maintain compliance with safety regulations and established procedures. Perform basic vehicle maintenance and cleaning tasks. Prioritize multiple responsibilities and respond effectively to emergencies or unexpected travel issues. Additional Information: The College of Wooster does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex/gender, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, political affiliation, religion, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, disability, age, marital status, family responsibilities, sexual orientation, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy, or by state, local, or federal law. All offers of employment are subject to verification of the legal right to work in the United States as required by federal law. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy . Application Instructions: For highest consideration please submit a resume, cover letter, and a list of 3 professional references which includes name, telephone number and email address. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation The College of Wooster 536 E. Wayne Ave, Wooster, OH 44691"
    },
    "https://wooster.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205036": {
      "title": "Director of Creative Services",
      "description": "The College of Wooster\nJob Posting: Director of Creative Services The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: Director of Creative Services Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Creative Services Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Marketing and Communications Locations: Wooster, OH Posted: Sep 21, 2026 Closes: Oct 25, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-time Exempt Position ID: 205036 Share About The College of Wooster: The College of Wooster is a vibrant community of Independent Minds, Working Together. The people who work at Wooster bring different experiences and perspectives to a collaborative environment united by a shared commitment to our students' success. Together, we support a distinctive liberal arts education built on close mentorship, intellectual curiosity, and opportunities for students to become creative, independent thinkers and problem-solvers. Whatever their role, our employees contribute their talents to the life of the College, connect with students and colleagues in meaningful ways, and help create a welcoming, supportive community where people can learn, grow, and thrive. Job Description: The Director of Creative Services provides strategic creative leadership across print, digital, web, social media, environmental, and branded applications. This role is responsible for conceptualization and implementation of design solutions for a wide range of digital and print collateral/assets that meet marketing strategies from concept to completion while being on brand, on time, and on budget. This position plays a lead role in developing integrated communications and ensuring compliance with College brand standards, collaborating with marketing, communications, content, digital, photography, and campus stakeholders to translate strategic goals into effective visual communications. This role oversees creative professionals, assigning and directing work to ensure high-quality work that meets the goals and objectives of deliverables. This role works closely with the Vice President of Marketing and Communications to optimize the design and use of The College of Wooster brand to a wide variety of targeted audiences, establish creative priorities, strengthen the College's brand presence, and improve creative processes. Essential Departmental Duties and Responsibilities: Collaborates with leadership to create annual marketing/communications plans, establish priorities, and identify creative strategies that advance College goals. Determines and creates designs for annual Admission and Advancement campaigns, Athletics creative and marketing initiatives, major College events and endeavors, and provides tools for general campus creative needs to ensure College brand standards are achieved. Leads and contributes to the visual direction, user experience, content presentation, accessibility, and brand consistency of the College's digital platforms and website in collaboration with digital, content, and marketing colleagues. Directs the creative workflow processes, including project intake, prioritization, scheduling, checking for accuracy of all formats and print proofs, and keeping records and archives consistent with department protocols. Serves as lead brand manager, providing input and ensuring established styles, fonts, logos, and marks are implemented consistently and with the highest level of design integrity. Ensures the identity guidelines are current and responsive to the College's needs. Creates templates and reference materials to support consistent use of brand. Reviews and approves licensed College-branded merchandise and artwork, including bookstore products, promotional items, and athletic uniforms, to ensure compliance with brand standards and visual identity guidelines. Works collaboratively with and serves as the main point of contact for print and merchandise vendors and creative freelancers, assuring accuracy, quality, and deadlines of project delivery and managing specifications, estimates, production schedules, proofs, and quality control. Coordinates all printing production, optimizing quality, cost effectiveness, consistency, production efficiency, and working within established budgets. Collaborates with photography, content and digital teams to identify visual needs, provide art direction, and optimize and curate the College's photo assets. Assigns and directs work of  creative talent to ensure production of high-quality, effective work, including providing direction, training, coaching, and following up on work results. Cultivates and mentors student interns to implement institutional designs and branding. Leads and/or participates in planning activities as a member of the Division of Marketing and Communications and acts as team lead for a variety of projects. Stays current with industry standards and trends related to design, digital, accessibility, production, technology, and higher education marketing - as well as industry tools and issues. This job has supervisory responsibilities for the creative team and student interns. Responsibilities include training and mentoring creative employees and student interns; planning, assigning, and directing work; providing feedback and professional development; and approving timesheets. Carries out supervisory responsibilities in accordance with the College's policies and applicable laws. Performs other duties as assigned. Requirements: Education and/or Experience: Bachelor's degree in graphic design, art, visual communications, marketing or related design field and a minimum of seven years of progressively responsible experience in graphic design, creative services, brand management, or visual communications within an in-house marketing and communications office, agency, higher education institution, or similarly complex organization. Demonstrated experience leading and project managing creative and integrated communications projects from concept through execution across print and digital channels, with a strong understanding of brand development, implementation, and stewardship. Demonstrated experience providing creative direction, managing complex workflows, collaborating with cross-functional teams, and supervising, coaching, or developing professional staff. Demonstrated experience with design software, project management software and digital asset management systems Knowledge Skills and Abilities: Skills: A portfolio demonstrating outstanding written, verbal, and communication skills, and ability to present ideas in a clear and concise manner. Demonstrated project management skills. Ability to build consensus across stakeholder groups and to work collaboratively as part of project teams made up of constituents across the College. Thrives in a fast-paced, dynamic environment with ability to prioritize and perform multiple tasks while maintaining close attention to detail and timeliness of work production. Brand management experience. Experience with mailing requirements. Demonstrated ability to use sound judgement in decision making and problem solving with strong organizational skills. Available to work a non-standard schedule in order to fulfill assigned duties and responsibilities around signature events. Knowledge: Demonstrated proficiency with Adobe Creative Cloud, with significant daily experience using Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign. Demonstrated proficiency with project management software (e.g., Monday.com, Trello) and digital asset management systems (e.g., Photoshelter) Experience with CRM/CMS platforms (e.g., Hubspot) Experience with Slate a plus Abilities: Acknowledge and comply with all departmental SOP, safety, and College requirements. Strong professional ethics and discretion with an attitude of respect for all employed at The College of Wooster and commitment to The College of Wooster's mission, vision, and values. Additional Information: The College of Wooster does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex/gender, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, political affiliation, religion, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, disability, age, marital status, family responsibilities, sexual orientation, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy, or by state, local, or federal law. All offers of employment are subject to verification of the legal right to work in the United States as required by federal law. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy . Application Instructions: For highest consideration please submit a resume, cover letter, portfolio, and a list of 3 professional references which includes name, telephone number and email address. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation The College of Wooster 536 E. Wayne Ave, Wooster, OH 44691"
    },
    "https://wooster.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203323": {
      "title": "General Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "The College of Wooster\nJob Posting: General Maintenance Technician The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: General Maintenance Technician Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details General Maintenance Technician Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Maintenance Operations Locations: Wooster, OH Posted: Aug 4, 2026 Closes: Nov 1, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position ID: 203323 Share About The College of Wooster: Wooster offers an excellent, comprehensive liberal arts education, culminating in a rigorous senior project, in which each student works one-on-one with a faculty mentor to conceive, organize and complete a significant research project on a topic of the student's own choosing. Through this distinctive program, every Wooster student develops abilities valued by employers and graduate schools alike: independent judgment, analytical ability, creativity, project-management and time-management skills, and strong written and oral communication skills. Founded in 1866, the college enrolls approximately 2,000 students. The College offers a comprehensive benefits program that includes: Health, Dental, Retirement, and Tuition Remission for eligible positions. Job Description: SUMMARY: Under general supervision, performs a variety of general maintenance duties which include mechanical, carpentry, and construction in the maintenance and repair of the college facilities, property, and equipment. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Complete maintenance service requests as assigned and in a timely manner. Assist Electricians, Plumbers, HVAC Technicians, and other staff members with routine maintenance activities. Inspect buildings, and equipment to ensure safe, well-maintained conditions, identify hazards, defects, and the need for adjustments or repair following up with a Web TMA service request. Perform troubleshooting and repair of roofing systems, wood structures, windows and screens, window blinds and shades, furniture, and other building components. Builds concrete forms for sidewalks and steps & finishes concrete. Assist with moving, loading, unloading and storing supplies, furniture and equipment. Identify and assist with carpentry- and repair work including painting, drywall installation and finishing/repair, batt and blown insulation, installs and repairs ceramic tile, interior and exterior trim, builds and repairs stair treads, risers, and handrails. Operate a variety of machinery, equipment and tools including saws, router, drills, sanders, planers, drill presses and various tools. Perform a variety of door hardware and controlled access equipment support, install new or repair existing locksets on doors, door closers, and panic hardware - requiring alteration to existing doors. Inspect, service and maintain operational functionality of doors and windows. May provide nuisance wildlife control through legal and proper means of containment and removal from campus buildings and structures. Participate in on call rotational process responding to campus needs for emergency calls outside of normal business hours including after hours, weekends, and holidays. Requirements: EDUCATION AND/OR EXPERIENCE: Certificate from a technical school in a building trade or apprenticeship and  three years related experience; or equivalent combination of education and experience. KNOWLEDGE SKILLS AND ABILITIES SKILLS Basic ability to read, interpret and work from blueprints, drawings, manufacturer Operations and Maintenance manuals, or oral instruction on a variety of structures and equipment related to building renovations and new construction. Communicate effectively in a professional, tactful and courteous manner with students, employees, faculty, and the general public. Ability to write routine reports and correspondence. Ability to speak effectively to staff, students, employees and outside contractors. KNOWLEDGE: Read and interpret documents such as blueprints, safety rules, operating and maintenance instructions, building codes, and procedure manuals. Wear proper protective equipment while performing job duties (i.e., safety glasses, hardhat, high viz safety vest, gloves, etc.). Thorough knowledge of local building codes. Must have valid Ohio driver's license. ABILITIES: Perform assigned responsibilities, duties, and tasks according to established practices, procedures, techniques, and standards in a safe manner and with minimal supervision. Acknowledge and comply with all departmental standard operating procedures (SOP), safety, and college requirements. Strong professional ethics and discretion with an attitude of respect for all employed at the college. Commitment to the college's mission, vision, and values. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this position, the staff member is regularly required to stand; walk; use hands, handle, or feel objects, tools, or controls; reach with hands and arms; climb or balance; stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl; and talk or hear. The employee is occasionally required to sit. The individual must regularly lift and/or move up to 25 pounds and occasionally lift and/or move up to 10 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this position include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and the ability to adjust focus. Additional Information: The College of Wooster does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex/gender, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, political affiliation, religion, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, disability, age, marital status, family responsibilities, sexual orientation, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy, or by state, local, or federal law. All offers of employment are subject to verification of the legal right to work in the United States as required by federal law. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy . Application Instructions: For highest consideration please submit a resume, cover letter, and a list of 3 professional references which includes name, telephone number and email address. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation The College of Wooster 536 E. Wayne Ave, Wooster, OH 44691"
    },
    "https://wooster.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205335": {
      "title": "High Pressure Boiler Operator",
      "description": "The College of Wooster\nJob Posting: High Pressure Boiler Operator The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: High Pressure Boiler Operator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details High Pressure Boiler Operator Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Power Plant & Utilities Locations: Wosoter, OH Posted: Sep 29, 2026 Closes: Oct 25, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position ID: 205335 Share About The College of Wooster: The College of Wooster is a vibrant community of Independent Minds, Working Together. The people who work at Wooster bring different experiences and perspectives to a collaborative environment united by a shared commitment to our students' success. Together, we support a distinctive liberal arts education built on close mentorship, intellectual curiosity, and opportunities for students to become creative, independent thinkers and problem-solvers. Whatever their role, our employees contribute their talents to the life of the College, connect with students and colleagues in meaningful ways, and help create a welcoming, supportive community where people can learn, grow, and thrive. Job Description: Summary: The High-Pressure Boiler Operator operates and maintains mechanical equipment such as boiler feed pumps, circulating pumps, water treatment equipment, air compressors, generators, motors, and natural gas fired steam boilers to generate steam and electricity for campus buildings. The High-Pressure Boiler Operator is in direct charge of all stationary engines and mechanical equipment and responsible for the continuous uninterrupted (24 hour / 7 day) safe and efficient operation of all systems and equipment. Participates in the maintenance, repair, rebuild, and new installation of equipment. Makes competent decisions regarding normal operations of the Powerhouse as well as emergency situations that may occur. Essential Departmental Duties and Responsibilities: Provides reliable steam and electrical supply to the campus by monitoring operating conditions, recording data, adjusting controls, inspecting and maintaining equipment. Maintains continuous operation of Powerhouse under various load and seasonal conditions, to assure the safe and efficient operations of all equipment. Performs water titration tests and adds appropriate chemical additives into treatment tanks to treat boiler waterside surfaces and distribution condensate return line. Performs other duties as assigned. Requirements: Education and/or Experience: High school diploma and one - three years verifiable experience operating and or maintaining boilers and boiler room equipment. Minimum requirement of a current High-Pressure Boiler Operator License issued by The State of Ohio. Knowledge Skills and Abilities: Skills: Strong problem solving and technical skills. Customer Service mindset. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work effectively independently and as a team member. Ability to read and interpret documents such as safety rules, operating and maintenance instructions, and procedure manuals. Ability to write routine reports and correspondence. Ability to speak effectively with staff members and employees of outside contractors/service companies. Knowledge: Uses computerized maintenance management system to provide work order status to customers. Ability to add, subtract, multiply, and divide in all units of measure, using whole numbers, common fractions, and decimals. Ability to compute rate, ratio, and percent and to interpret charts and graphs. Abilities: Acknowledge and comply with all departmental SOP, safety, and college requirements. Strong professional ethics and discretion with an attitude of respect for all employed at the College of Wooster. Additional Information: The College of Wooster does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex/gender, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, political affiliation, religion, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, disability, age, marital status, family responsibilities, sexual orientation, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy, or by state, local, or federal law. All offers of employment are subject to verification of the legal right to work in the United States as required by federal law. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy . Application Instructions: For highest consideration please submit a resume, cover letter, and a list of 3 professional references which includes name, telephone number and email address. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation The College of Wooster 536 E. Wayne Ave, Wooster, OH 44691"
    },
    "https://wooster.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205928": {
      "title": "Marketing Communications Strategist",
      "description": "The College of Wooster\nJob Posting: Marketing Communications Strategist The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: Marketing Communications Strategist Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Marketing Communications Strategist Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Marketing and Communications Locations: Wooster, OH Posted: Oct 19, 2026 Closes: Nov 22, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Full-time Exempt Position ID: 205928 Share About The College of Wooster: The College of Wooster is a vibrant community of Independent Minds, Working Together. The people who work at Wooster bring different experiences and perspectives to a collaborative environment united by a shared commitment to our students' success. Together, we support a distinctive liberal arts education built on close mentorship, intellectual curiosity, and opportunities for students to become creative, independent thinkers and problem-solvers. Whatever their role, our employees contribute their talents to the life of the College, connect with students and colleagues in meaningful ways, and help create a welcoming, supportive community where people can learn, grow, and thrive. Job Description: Summary: The Marketing Communications Strategist develops compelling marketing strategies, messaging, and content that advance the College's strategic priorities, with a primary emphasis on undergraduate enrollment marketing while also supporting advancement, alumni and family engagement, academic programs, and other institutional initiatives. Reporting to the Vice President of Marketing, Communications & Events, this position serves as the division's subject matter expert in enrollment marketing and persuasive communications. Working as part of a collaborative, agency-style marketing team, the Marketing Communications Strategist develops campaign messaging, content strategies, and marketing materials that engage key audiences across print and digital channels. The position partners closely with Creative Services, Digital Marketing and Social Media, Communications, and campus stakeholders to translate institutional priorities into effective marketing campaigns that support enrollment, strengthen the College's brand and support measurable institutional goals. Essential Departmental Duties and Responsibilities: Marketing Strategy & Content Development Collaborate with the Director of Creative Services, Director of Digital Marketing and campus partners to develop integrated marketing strategies supporting institutional priorities. Develop audience-centered messaging frameworks and content strategies for enrollment, advancement, alumni engagement, and other initiatives. Serve as a subject matter expert in undergraduate enrollment marketing and recruitment communications. Recommend marketing tactics and communication approaches aligned with campaign objectives and institutional priorities. Write, edit, and refine persuasive marketing copy for print and digital communications. Content Creation & Storytelling Create compelling content for websites, landing pages, recruitment publications, email campaigns, digital advertising, brochures, alumni and advancement communications, student and faculty profiles, presentations, and video scripts. Develop editorial plans that support integrated marketing campaigns. Identify and develop authentic stories that demonstrate the value and impact of a Wooster education. Ensure all messaging reflects the College's brand voice and positioning. Website & Digital Content Maintain and update marketing content using the College's content management system. Recommend improvements to user experience, accessibility, SEO, and content organization. Partner with Digital Marketing to support campaign landing pages and digital initiatives. Creative Collaboration Partner with designers, photographers, videographers, digital marketers, communicators, and event professionals to develop integrated marketing initiatives. Contribute marketing expertise throughout the creative development process. Collaborate effectively within a multidisciplinary marketing team. Requirements: Education and/or Experience: Bachelor's degree in marketing, communications, journalism, public relations, or a related field. A minimum of seven years of experience with three years in a similar role in higher ed marketing, communications, or content strategy. Exceptional writing, editing, and proofreading skills. Demonstrated experience developing persuasive marketing communications and audience-centered campaigns. Knowledge Skills and Abilities: Skills: Experience in undergraduate enrollment marketing or admissions communications and skill in interpreting data/analyzing campaign results. Outstanding storytelling and persuasive writing skills. A history of progressively responsible roles. Strong project management, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Knowledge: Experience with: content management systems such as Hubspot;  Adobe Creative Cloud or comparable design tools; email marketing platforms; SEO and AI-enabled search strategies; accessibility; and digital analytics. Abilities: Understanding of content strategy, audience engagement, and enrollment marketing best practices. Ability to manage multiple priorities while collaborating across creative, digital, communications, social media and events teams. Commitment to brand consistency and high-quality creative work. Additional Information: The College of Wooster does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex/gender, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, political affiliation, religion, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, disability, age, marital status, family responsibilities, sexual orientation, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy, or by state, local, or federal law. All offers of employment are subject to verification of the legal right to work in the United States as required by federal law. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy . Application Instructions: For highest consideration please submit a resume, cover letter, and a list of 3 professional references which includes name, telephone number and email address. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation The College of Wooster 536 E. Wayne Ave, Wooster, OH 44691"
    },
    "https://wooster.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204765": {
      "title": "Safety Officer",
      "description": "The College of Wooster\nJob Posting: Safety Officer The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: Safety Officer Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Safety Officer Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Security & Protective Services Locations: Wooster, OH Posted: Sep 13, 2026 Closes: Nov 1, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position ID: 204765 Share About The College of Wooster: Wooster offers an excellent, comprehensive liberal arts education, culminating in a rigorous senior project, in which each student works one-on-one with a faculty mentor to conceive, organize and complete a significant research project on a topic of the student's own choosing. Through this distinctive program, every Wooster student develops abilities valued by employers and graduate schools alike: independent judgment, analytical ability, creativity, project-management and time-management skills, and strong written and oral communication skills. Founded in 1866, the college enrolls approximately 2,000 students. The College offers a comprehensive benefits program that includes: Health, Dental, Retirement, and Tuition Remission for eligible positions. Job Description: Summary: The Safety Officer is responsible for ensuring the safety and security of the campus community, including students, faculty, staff, and visitors. This role involves patrolling campus property, responding to emergencies and calls for service, enforcing campus policies and procedures, promoting a safe and secure campus environment through visibility, communication, and proactive engagement. While the position is primarily patrol and response-based, officers may also be assigned to administrative and dispatch duties as needed. Essential Departmental Duties and Responsibilities: Conduct regular patrols (foot, vehicle, building) to deter crime, identify safety concerns, and secure facilities. Respond to incidents, alarms, and emergencies with professionalism and urgency, including medical and evacuation situations. Monitor and report suspicious activity, safety hazards, and policy violations. Enforce campus rules and regulations fairly and consistently. Write detailed incident reports and maintain accurate documentation and department logs. Maintain clear radio communication with dispatch and officers; perform dispatch duties as needed. Assist in investigations and follow-up activities in coordination with relevant personnel. Support community policing efforts by providing safety escorts and serving as a visible, approachable presence. Participate in safety drills and training and collaborate with emergency services and campus staff. Perform administrative tasks such as data entry, filing, and updating schedules; work flexible hours as assigned. Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements: Education and/or Experience: High school diploma or equivalent required; associate or bachelor's degree (BA) in criminal justice, law enforcement or related field preferred. Consideration will be given for related experience and/or training or equivalent combination Previous experience in campus safety, security, law enforcement, or a related field preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Skills: Technical competency: Basic computer skills and familiarity with safety reporting systems and administrative tools. Excellent communication skills: Strong written and verbal abilities, with experience in preparing reports and professional correspondence. Attention to detail: Dependable with strong observational skills and a commitment to accuracy in documentation and reporting Abilities: Sound judgment and reliability: Demonstrates integrity, professionalism, situational awareness, and the ability to remain calm under pressure. Policy and procedure proficiency: Capable of independently interpreting and applying guidelines, instructions, and operating procedures. Abilities: Valid Ohio driver's license and clean driving record Ability to pass a background check, physical, and training requirements (e.g., CPR, First Aid, report writing, de-escalation) Interpersonal effectiveness: Able to interact respectfully and effectively, skilled in customer service, teamwork, and de-escalation. Additional Information: The College of Wooster does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex/gender, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, political affiliation, religion, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, disability, age, marital status, family responsibilities, sexual orientation, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy, or by state, local, or federal law. All offers of employment are subject to verification of the legal right to work in the United States as required by federal law. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy . Application Instructions: For highest consideration please submit a resume, cover letter, and a list of 3 professional references which includes name, telephone number and email address. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation The College of Wooster 536 E. Wayne Ave, Wooster, OH 44691"
    },
    "https://wooster.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204201": {
      "title": "Senior Accountant, Grants and General Ledger",
      "description": "The College of Wooster\nJob Posting: Senior Accountant, Grants and General Ledger The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: Senior Accountant, Grants and General Ledger Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Senior Accountant, Grants and General Ledger Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Business Office Locations: Wooster, OH Posted: Aug 27, 2026 Closes: Oct 31, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-time Exempt Position ID: 204201 Share About The College of Wooster: Wooster offers an excellent, comprehensive liberal arts education, culminating in a rigorous senior project, in which each student works one-on-one with a faculty mentor to conceive, organize and complete a significant research project on a topic of the student's own choosing. Through this distinctive program, every Wooster student develops abilities valued by employers and graduate schools alike: independent judgment, analytical ability, creativity, project-management and time-management skills, and strong written and oral communication skills. Founded in 1866, the college enrolls approximately 2,000 students. The College offers a comprehensive benefits program that includes: Health, Dental, Retirement, and Tuition Remission for eligible positions. Job Description: SUMMARY: The Senior Accountant, Grants and General Ledger is responsible for the accounting, administration and financial oversight of all College grants; primarily federal research grants and private grants from corporations and foundations. This position creates and monitors grant-related budgets. This position ensures timely and accurate grant reporting for all federal, state, local and non-government grants. The Senior Accountant, Grants and General Ledger oversees all grant-related cash receipts and the completion of related month-end, quarter-end and year-end journal entries for grant accounts. This position is responsible for fixed asset accounting and has responsibility for certain recurring journal entries including departmental recharges, prepaid accounts, accruals in coordination with the Assistant Controller. This position is also responsible for accounting for restricted scholarships. The position actively assists the Assistant Controller and AVP/Controller in the preparation of year-end financial statements in accordance with GAAP. ESSENTIAL DEPARTMENTAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Grants Accounting Supports pre-award grant activities by assisting with budget development, budget justifications, proposal transmittals, and grant budget submissions in collaboration with Associate Director of Sponsored Research. Manages all post-award grant administration, including financial accounting, expenditure monitoring, compliance oversight, and preparation of grant reports and quarterly and annual financial reports for the College's grant portfolio. Ensures compliance with federal, state, local, grantor, and institutional regulations and policies governing grants, including Uniform Guidance (2 CFR 200), and provides analysis and guidance on grant-related financial matters. Assists with indirect cost rate proposals and negotiations, Assists with grant, audit and regulatory reporting requirements, year-end financial statements (e.g., Uniform Guidance audit, financial compliance reviews, NSF Survey, SEFA, F&A proposal development), and the development and maintenance of grant policies and procedures. General Accounting Responsible for fixed asset accounting, including capitalization, depreciation, disposals, and reconciliations. Prepares and posts recurring journal entries, including departmental recharges, prepaid expense amortization and others as assigned. Supports month-end and year-end closing processes by ensuring all assigned journal entries, reconciliations, and accounting adjustments are completed accurately and within established deadlines. Actively assists the Assistant Controller and AVP/Controller in the preparation of year-end financial statements in accordance with GAAP and completion of the annual audit. Serves as back-up to Accounts Payable Manager. Assists with other duties and projects as assigned by the Associate Vice President & Controller or the Vice President for Finance and Business. Requirements: EDUCATION AND/OR EXPERIENCE: Minimum 3 years of experience in grants and general ledger accounting. Not-for-profit or higher education experience. Bachelor's degree in accounting, finance or related field; CPA preferred Experience with Datatel's Colleague software Proven ability to understand grant applicant (PI) needs, requirements and requests to identify priorities. KNOWLEDGE SKILLS AND ABILITIES SKILLS: Critical thinking and problem-solving skills. Adept at navigating complex environments with evolving priorities and communication plans. Professional and interpersonal skills and an ability to communicate effectively in person, writing, and over the phone. KNOWLEDGE: Ability to add, subtract, multiply, and divide in all units of measure, using whole numbers, common fractions, and decimals. Ability to compute rate, ratio, and percent. Must be detail-oriented with the ability to process a large amount of data with complete accuracy. Proficiency in Microsoft Office 365; Advanced Excel skills. ABILITIES: Must be able to keep information confidential. Acknowledge and comply with all departmental SOP, safety, and College requirements. Commitment to the College's mission, vision, and values Additional Information: The College of Wooster does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex/gender, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, political affiliation, religion, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, disability, age, marital status, family responsibilities, sexual orientation, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy, or by state, local, or federal law. All offers of employment are subject to verification of the legal right to work in the United States as required by federal law. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy . Application Instructions: For highest consideration please submit a resume, cover letter, and a list of 3 professional references which includes name, telephone number and email address. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation The College of Wooster 536 E. Wayne Ave, Wooster, OH 44691"
    },
    "https://wooster.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203950": {
      "title": "Video and Multimedia Production Manager",
      "description": "The College of Wooster\nJob Posting: Video and Multimedia Production Manager The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: Video and Multimedia Production Manager Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Video and Multimedia Production Manager Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Marketing and Communications Locations: Wooster, OH Posted: Aug 20, 2026 Closes: Oct 25, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-time Exempt Position ID: 203950 Share About The College of Wooster: Wooster offers an excellent, comprehensive liberal arts education, culminating in a rigorous senior project, in which each student works one-on-one with a faculty mentor to conceive, organize and complete a significant research project on a topic of the student's own choosing. Through this distinctive program, every Wooster student develops abilities valued by employers and graduate schools alike: independent judgment, analytical ability, creativity, project-management and time-management skills, and strong written and oral communication skills. Founded in 1866, the college enrolls approximately 2,000 students. The College offers a comprehensive benefits program that includes: Health, Dental, Retirement, and Tuition Remission for eligible positions. Job Description: Summary: The Video and Multimedia Producer leads the creation of compelling, distinctive, and inspiring branding video, audio, and motion graphic content that tells the story of the College. Through strategic visual storytelling, this position engages prospective and current students, families, alumni, donors, faculty, and staff while elevating the College's reputation and advancing institutional priorities. This position conceives, develops, and produces creative multimedia solutions that support College initiatives and strategic goals across digital, social, and advertising channels. The Video and Multimedia Producer creates engaging, audience-focused content, measures its effectiveness using analytics, and applies insights to continuously improve future productions. Working collaboratively with colleagues across campus, the Video and Multimedia Producer also manages student interns, coordinates freelance creative partners as needed and helps provide experiential learning opportunities that enhance students' professional development. Essential Departmental Duties and Responsibilities: Produces, shoots, and edits high-quality video and multimedia content for the College's website, social media, digital advertising, events, and other communications channels. Plans and executes all phases of video production, including storyboarding, scriptwriting, scheduling, talent coordination, location scouting, filming, audio recording, lighting, and post-production editing, including motion graphics, captioning, and platform-specific formatting. Conducts interviews with students, faculty, staff, alumni, donors, trustees, and other stakeholders to capture authentic stories that support the College's marketing and communications efforts. Identifies opportunities to create multimedia content that promotes the College, highlights institutional priorities, and increases audience engagement, while collaborating with the marketing and communications team on creative campaigns and content initiatives. Ensures all video content meets accessibility standards through captioning and other appropriate accommodations. Organizes, maintains, and expands the College's digital media library, including finished productions, b-roll, photography, and archival footage, ensuring assets are properly cataloged, stored, and easily retrievable. Develops and maintains efficient production workflows, file management systems, and archival procedures to support ongoing multimedia production. Monitors content performance using analytics and applies insights to improve future multimedia projects and audience engagement. Trains and supervises student interns, providing meaningful experiential learning opportunities while ensuring high-quality project support. Manages relationships with freelance creative professionals and coordinates external production resources as needed.  Oversees the inventory, maintenance, storage, and replacement planning of the College's video production equipment and ensures the College's YouTube channel remains current, organized, and optimized. Stays current with emerging trends, technologies, and best practices in video production, multimedia storytelling, and content distribution through ongoing professional development. Performs other duties as assigned. Requirements: Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Education and/or Experience: Bachelor's degree in broadcast journalism, video production, multimedia production, visual production, visual communications, or related field, from a four-year college or university. Knowledge Skills and Abilities: Skills: Demonstrated skill and experience in video shooting, editing and production, from ideation to finished product, as evidenced by a portfolio of work. Track record of producing high-end imagery for use across the marketing and communications spectrum. Experience overseeing or mentoring staff or student interns. Demonstrated project management ability, managing multiple projects at once and working on deadlines. Broad knowledge of social media video content, multiple formats and styles of short-form storytelling. Photography experience and/or drone licensure a plus. Available to periodically work a non-standard schedule to fulfill assigned duties and responsibilities in accordance with college events. Knowledge: Outstanding written and verbal communication skills Ability to demonstrate leadership and exercise diplomacy, professionalism, consensus building, and discretion with college stakeholders High level of proficiency and experience with the Adobe Creative Suite, including but not limited to Premiere Pro and After Effects or other animation tools, like DaVinci Resolve. Abilities: Acknowledge and comply with all departmental SOP, safety, and College requirements. Commitment to the College's mission, vision, and values. Additional Information: The College of Wooster does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex/gender, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, political affiliation, religion, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, disability, age, marital status, family responsibilities, sexual orientation, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy, or by state, local, or federal law. All offers of employment are subject to verification of the legal right to work in the United States as required by federal law. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy . Application Instructions: For highest consideration, please submit the following application materials: Resume Cover letter Video production portfolio and/or demo reel List of three professional references, including each reference's name, telephone number, and email address Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation The College of Wooster 536 E. Wayne Ave, Wooster, OH 44691"
    },
    "https://wooster.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206210": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President & Controller",
      "description": "The College of Wooster\nJob Posting: Associate Vice President & Controller The College of Wooster \n\tJob Posting: Associate Vice President & Controller Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Vice President & Controller Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Business Office Locations: Wooster, OH Posted: Oct 28, 2026 Closes: Nov 29, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Full-time Exempt Position ID: 206210 Share About The College of Wooster: The College of Wooster is a vibrant community of Independent Minds, Working Together. The people who work at Wooster bring different experiences and perspectives to a collaborative environment united by a shared commitment to our students' success. Together, we support a distinctive liberal arts education built on close mentorship, intellectual curiosity, and opportunities for students to become creative, independent thinkers and problem-solvers. Whatever their role, our employees contribute their talents to the life of the College, connect with students and colleagues in meaningful ways, and help create a welcoming, supportive community where people can learn, grow, and thrive. Job Description: Summary: The Associate Vice President & Controller oversees the College's day-to-day financial operations, leading the Business Office team. This role is pivotal in managing the monthly and annual closing of accounting records and preparing the College's financial statements. The Associate Vice President & Controller ensures the timely and accurate completion of the College's 990 and 990-T tax returns. Collaborating closely with the Finance Director and Finance Manager of Budget, Reporting, and Analysis, they assist in monitoring actual results and provide insights to inform projections. Additionally, this position is responsible for maintaining robust internal controls to safeguard College assets and ensuring compliance with all federal, state, and local regulations. This role also plays a critical leadership role in advancing the College's finance and business process modernization, data strategy and operational excellence initiatives. Essential Departmental Duties and Responsibilities: Ensures accurate, efficient, and well-controlled processing of financial transactions through optimized and automated workflows. Oversees the Accounts Receivable and Accounts Payable functions for the college. Oversees Endowment accounting and responsible for initiating investment manager transactions. Oversees cash management and initiation of banking transactions. Responsible for the preparation of the annual financial statements. Coordinates the annual financial statement and Uniform Guidance audits with the independent auditor. Oversees processes which ensure that all federal Title IV federal money is handled according to federal regulations, in conjunction with Director of Financial Aid. Oversee Grants Accounting for the College's Federal State and Private Research grants. Oversees the completion of the annual Form 990 & 990T and related State tax returns. Prepare all necessary bond disclosure documents and assist the Vice President for Finance and Business with new bond issues when needed; ensure compliance with Bond covenants for existing bonds; Help to design and implement financial policies and procedures. Implement and continually review financial internal control systems. Leads optimization of end-to-end business processes; Identifies and implements business process improvements across accounting, reporting, and close cycles to reduce manual effort and cycle times. Helps to ensure that short-term cash is invested according to the College's investment policy. Supports the Audit & Risk, Investment, and Resources Committees of the Board of Trustees. Ensures that the College is adhering to all federal, state, local laws and regulations that impact the college's operations. Assist with the preparation of the annual IPEDS report, NACUBO endowment study, federal and state department of education reporting and other various reports and surveys. Evaluates and implements emerging technologies to improve efficiency, accuracy and scalability. Builds and develops a high-performing accounting and business office team. Assists with other duties as assigned by the Vice President for Finance and Business Requirements: Education and/or Experience : Bachelor's Degree in accounting and CPA; ten years minimum accounting experience in complex organization (not-for-profit preferred) Strong communication and organization skills Advanced proficiency in ERP systems, reporting tools, Microsoft Office Suite skills Experience with automation and AI-enabled finance solutions preferred Significant experience overseeing accounting and business teams, directing workflows, and ensuring achievement of departmental deadlines Proven ability to lead, coach, and develop accounting professionals while driving engagement, accountability, and high-quality financial execution Knowledge Skills and Abilities: Skills: Ability to read, analyze, and interpret general office policies, technical procedures, accounting guidance or governmental regulations. Ability to author reports, business correspondence, and procedure manuals. Ability to develop and manage workplans. Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from Board, Cabinet, parents, students, and staff members. Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables. Must be able to present information in repetitive situations with courtesy, tact, and interest. Must be detail-oriented, with the ability to process a large amount of data with complete accuracy. Knowledge: Ability to add, subtract, multiply, and divide in all units of measure, using whole numbers, common fractions, and decimals. Ability to compute rate, ratio, and percentage. Abilities: Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information with discretion. Additional Information: The College of Wooster does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex/gender, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, political affiliation, religion, creed, ethnicity, national origin (including ancestry), citizenship status, disability, age, marital status, family responsibilities, sexual orientation, veteran or military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, domestic violence victim status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy, or by state, local, or federal law. All offers of employment are subject to verification of the legal right to work in the United States as required by federal law. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy. For more information see our nondiscrimination policy . Application Instructions: For highest consideration please submit a resume, cover letter, and a list of 3 professional references which includes name, telephone number and email address. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation The College of Wooster 536 E. Wayne Ave, Wooster, OH 44691"
    }
